                <pb facs="0967" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.51/408: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spencer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-03T19:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                                1920—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>77. Semiofficial newspaper published yesterday afternoon <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >acuerdo</hi> dated October 23 fixing War Department expenditures for
                    November at 166,000 pesos representing probable economy of over 200,000 compared
                    with recent months. Government adopted these projects with only minor
                    alterations and considers complete adoption of reformed budget with important
                    economies in other departments during this week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spencer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
